[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"463","stub":{"id":"463","section":"Anneewakee Road to GA Route 166","altname":"","river":"Annewakee","difficulty":"IItoIIIplusstandoutIV","states":["USA-GEO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"116","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"This river wide hole makes a great warm-up spot. The river left side is a cool seam. The river right side is a bigger hole/wave with great play, However... it's quite difficult to make a graceful exit from this side.","id":"223","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Put In Hole","distance":"0","photoID":"1633","difficulty":"III","approximate":false},{"type":"waterfall","description":"This is the first big drop on the creek. Pull over on river left bank to scout this one. The drop is safe all the way across however... There will be an ugly hole awaiting you quickly below the drop if you go off too far to the right. Stick to the left.","id":"440","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"AnneWakeup!","distance":"0.75","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"1634"},{"type":"playspot","description":"Powerline rapid drops over a series of rock shelves creating fun drops and good surfing waves. Eddy out at the bottom on the right before the horizon line. You'll want to scout the next drop.","id":"441","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"PowerLine","distance":"0.9","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"1635"},{"type":"hazard","description":"Right off the center seems to be the way to go here. Too far left is pinning potential. Left of center lands you on a rock shelf. Right of center puts you into the meat. Far right is a possibility. The bulk of the water pours over here and plunges into the abyss... I'd like to see it at lower water before running it. Paddle hard after the drop or the base of the falls will pull you in. After the big drop you still have some manuevering to do. Portage is on river right.","id":"442","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"PowerSLAM!","distance":"1","photoID":"1546","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"115375","location":{"latitude":"33.6652984619141","longitude":"-84.6837997436523"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"3.5","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101248913","title":null,"post_date":"2011-11-28 05:00:00+00","detail":"There is a lot of wood in the river below PowerSlam. Some of it is passable but some of it is not. Make sure you can see the next safe eddy before you paddle around bends. And when you come to a sharp left turn after Powerslide that requires you to squeeze between a couple of trees to get into the next channel---don't, it gets worse, just start the portage.","user":{"name":"Chris Robinson"}}],"photos":[{"id":"1542","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"Mike & Dale paddling through the playspot-rich Powerline Rapid","caption":"Annewakee PowerLine","poi_name":"PowerLine","subject":"Mike & Dale","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1542","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1542"}},{"id":"1549","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"I think a creekboat would have been able to pull away from this but a Disco.... Uh, no.","caption":"This is NOT good","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"Mike","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1549","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1549"}},{"id":"1544","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"This is the biggest rapid on the run.  Running far river left was NOT an option. The hole at the bottom is strong.","caption":"Annewakee PowerSLAM!","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1544","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1544"}},{"id":"1551","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"As soon as he started to wash free, Mike decided to go for a swim.  Not a good place to swim.  Dale gets ready to throw him a rope.","caption":"He's Out!","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"Mike","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1551","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1551"}},{"id":"1634","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4157","description":"This is the first big drop on the creek.  Run this river left to avoid the river right/center hole after the drop.","caption":"AnneWakeup!","poi_name":"AnneWakeup!","subject":"1st big drop on the creek","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"440","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1634","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1634"}},{"id":"4069","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken","caption":"[0013] Below PowerSlam!","poi_name":"PowerSlam!","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"223","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4069","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4069"}},{"id":"4071","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken\r\nthis exploding wave is cause by an undercut/boulder seive that is normally well out of the water.  very nasty!","caption":"[0013] Exploding wave at PowerSlam!","poi_name":"PowerSlam","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"223","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4071","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4071"}},{"id":"4073","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken\r\nif this ledge looks really scrapy it's probably too low...if it looks side surfable it's good to go...play-able is really good...and when it washses out into a wave it's too high for most of us","caption":"[0013] level indicator ledge/hole/wave at putin","poi_name":"Put0in","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"223","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4073","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4073"}},{"id":"10741","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8205","description":"<p>There is a big rock causing that boil but there is a nice pillow that will push you off of it if you get over there. For more \r\nVisit <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.lithiumkayaking.com\">Lithium Kayaking</a></p>\r\n","caption":"There's a rock in there!!","poi_name":"Trolly (3rd major rapid)","subject":"David Holcomb","author":"Dallas Shaw","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10741","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10741"}},{"id":"10742","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8205","description":"<p>This run is full of strainers now. Some in bad spots. For more \r\nVisit <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.lithiumkayaking.com\">Lithium Kayaking</a></p>\r\n","caption":"Usual scene on Annawakee","poi_name":"Strainer #6,732","subject":"1 of the many strainers","author":"Dallas Shaw","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10742","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10742"}},{"id":"1540","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"Sweetwater Creek (Online Guage) reached 4ft. that day.  This is the 1st big drop on the run","caption":"Annewakee 1st Drop","poi_name":"1st Drop","subject":"Mike Leal","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1540","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1540"}},{"id":"4064","ext":"mov","post_id":"4625","description":"","caption":"[0013] Last Big Rapid","poi_name":"Last Big Rapid","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4064","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4064"}},{"id":"4070","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken.\r\nthere was a strainer at this level on far right...probablly  not an issue at lower levels","caption":"[0013] Last Big Rapid","poi_name":"???","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4070","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4070"}},{"id":"10738","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8205","description":"<p>We think that the flow peaked about the time we were at powerslam. There was debri hung up on the top of the bridge support when we got back but the water had come back down to the red line. Very flashy creek. For more \r\nVisit <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.lithiumkayaking.com\">Lithium Kayaking</a></p>\r\n","caption":"And Rising!!!","poi_name":"Guage","subject":"Gauge","author":"Dallas Shaw","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10738","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10738"}},{"id":"18166","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9636","description":"It was low..... that's all.","caption":"Low water","poi_name":"??","subject":"Terran","author":"Dallas","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18166","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18166"}},{"id":"1632","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"","caption":"PowerSLAM!","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"Mike","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1632","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1632"}},{"id":"1550","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"Not a good situation to be in.","caption":"Where'd he go??","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"Mike","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1550","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1550"}},{"id":"1548","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"The shallow rock shelf has pointed poor mike a little far to the right :(","caption":"Headed for Trouble","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"Mike","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1548","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1548"}},{"id":"1547","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"Shallow rock shelf... SLAM! It gets ugly from here.","caption":"SLAM!","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"Mike","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1547","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1547"}},{"id":"1546","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"Mike demonstrates excellent form mid-drop.","caption":"Mike has great form !!","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"Mike","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1546","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1546"}},{"id":"1545","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"Mike getting ready to run the middle line on PowerSLAM!","caption":"Mike sets up for PowerSLAM!","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"Mike ","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1545","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1545"}},{"id":"1543","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"About to drop into 1 of the many great waves in PowerLine on Annewakee Creek.","caption":"Annewakee PowerLine Wave","poi_name":"PowerLine","subject":"Patrick Dortch","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1543","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1543"}},{"id":"1541","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"Me playing in and trying to stay clear of the other side of PutIn Hole.","caption":"Annewakee Putin Hole","poi_name":"Putin Hole","subject":"Me in the hole","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"442","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1541","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1541"}},{"id":"1552","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4154","description":"Mike throws in the towel and heads for shore.. Hey mike, where's your boat going??  2 miles downstream. THIS has been a Disastro moment.","caption":"Hey, where's your boat going?","poi_name":"PowerSLAM!","subject":"Mike","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"441","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1552","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1552"}},{"id":"1635","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4156","description":"This is a fun section.  There's lots of waves and good boogie water.","caption":"Powerline Rapid","poi_name":"Powerline","subject":"Mike & Dale in Powerline rapid","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"442","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1635","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1635"}},{"id":"1633","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4157","description":"Looking at the strong side of the hole.","caption":"You want me to go where?","poi_name":"Put In Hole","subject":"Patrick Dortch","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":"442","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1633","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1633"}},{"id":"4063","ext":"mov","post_id":"4625","description":"","caption":"[0013] Powerslam!","poi_name":"Powerslam!","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"223","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4063","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4063"}},{"id":"4062","ext":"mov","post_id":"4625","description":"","caption":"[0013] Powerline Rapids","poi_name":"Powerline","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"442","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4062","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4062"}},{"id":"4065","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken","caption":"[0013] AnneWakeUp","poi_name":"AnneWakeUp","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"440","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4065","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4065"}},{"id":"4067","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken","caption":"[0013] Nice wave at top of Powerline Rapids","poi_name":"Powerline","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"442","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4067","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4067"}},{"id":"4068","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken","caption":"[0013] PowerSlam!","poi_name":"PowerSlam!","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"223","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4068","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4068"}},{"id":"4061","ext":"mov","post_id":"4625","description":"","caption":"[0013] Annawakee","poi_name":"Annewakeup!","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"440","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4061","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4061"}},{"id":"4072","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken","caption":"[0013] above PowerSlam!","poi_name":"PowerSlam!","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"223","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4072","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4072"}},{"id":"4074","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken\r\nnotice the water well out of the banks.  the water was 1ft below the bottom of the bridge support when I got there and the water just barely out of the banks.","caption":"[0013] Level indicator at put-in","poi_name":"Put-in","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"223","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4074","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4074"}},{"id":"4066","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4625","description":"sweetwater peaked at 11.8ft right when these pics were taken","caption":"[0013] Hole below AnneWakeUp","poi_name":"AnneWakeUp","subject":"","author":"Chad Spangler","poi_id":"440","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4066","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4066"}},{"id":"10737","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8205","description":"<p>Great boof. I forgot this guys name so if anyone knows him let me know. For more \r\nVisit <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.lithiumkayaking.com\">Lithium Kayaking</a></p>\r\n","caption":"AnneWakeUp","poi_name":"AnneWakeUp","subject":"EZ (forgot the guys name)","author":"Dallas Shaw","poi_id":"440","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10737","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10737"}},{"id":"10739","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8205","description":"<p>What a great run. Annawakee went above the red line on this run. For more \r\nVisit <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.lithiumkayaking.com\">Lithium Kayaking</a></p>\r\n","caption":"Uh Oh","poi_name":"PowerSlam","subject":"EZ (forgot his name)","author":"Dallas Shaw","poi_id":"442","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10739","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10739"}},{"id":"10740","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8205","description":"<p>That's me on PowerSlam. This is a fun drop but the holes are very retentive. For more \r\nVisit <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.lithiumkayaking.com\">Lithium Kayaking</a></p>\r\n","caption":"Yee Haw","poi_name":"PowerSlam","subject":"Dallas Shaw","author":"EZ","poi_id":"442","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10740","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10740"}}],"detail":{"id":"463","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"## Gauge Description\n\nLook for Sweetwater Creek to be runing 800 cfs and **rising** or locally heavy rain of at least 1.25 inches.\n\n**Annewakke will drop back down to nothing in a matter of hours.** The sweetwater gauge is used to show if Annewakkee has gotten enough rain to check, but sweetwater holds water for days.\n\n**River Description:**\n\nThe put-in is on Annewakee Road and there's good parking on the downstream side of the bridge. There is a great but grabby playspot right at the putin. The creek picks up quickly and gets your blood pumping with a few fun class 2's. Then it's flat for a bit... then the horizon line. The first large drop is about 9 feet and reminds me of the Upper Tellico. It's a safe drop if run left of center, look out for the \"Hole of Doom\" on the center-right after the main drop. It probably wouldn't kill you but you'd probably swim out. It's easy to miss.\n\nNext is a short class 2-3 section that runs through a power line cut. There are some great waves here! You used to be able to drive (4x4 only!) out the power lines to this spot but thanks to vandals the entrance has been cabled off.\n\nBe VERY careful not to just drop over the next horizon line immediatley after the power lines, you could get REALLY hurt. The next drop is about a 12 footer and really kicks. The river left side is an almost certain pin. The water runs down a slide and hits a jagged rock and forms a kind of mini Oceana with a not-so-forgiving \"Thing\". The left of center line has rocks at the bottom so that's no good. The center line seems the way to go, angling to the right a bit.. Be careful not to get sucked back into the hole at the bottom or you're swimming. The right side could be OK but we didn't run it. The far right side is a plunge into the abyss and we didn't know what was down there so it's still a mystery. The portage is on river right.\n\nAfter the big drop there is a 1/4 mile of class 3 water with a fun double drop that's a strong III+ at normal levels and turns into solid 4 at high flow. After this, the river takes a sharp turn to the right and slows down for a mile or so. Then it takes a hard turn to the left and cuts through another ridge, the action picks up here again and a few class 2's and 3's appear but nothing like the upper section. A bit of flat water gets you to the take out on Ga 166.\n\nThis is a great run! We were very impressed. The water quality is not great but the rapids are! As of March 2002 there were a few dead falls that needed to be carried over but no \"strainers of doom\".\n\nFYI, Sweetwater reached almost 4 feet that day after rain the night before and Annewakee was at a comfortable level. It could certainly be done higher, but not much lower. Total rainfall for the previous night was about 1.2 inches and it was still raining lightly when we put on at 2pm. It will take you between 1.5 to 2.5 hours to make this run barring any epic adventures.","averageGradient":"30","maxGradient":"100","length":"3.7","correlations":[{"reachID":"463","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"800","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"4000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"SWEETWATER CREEK NEAR AUSTELL, GA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"02337000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value"